{"remedy_type":"claude-md","failure_statement":"The agent modifies or touches parts of the codebase the user explicitly excluded from scope (e.g., "don't touch tests," "leave the formatter alone," "no network calls"), apparently losing track of the constraint mid-task rather than checking its changes against it before finishing.","remedy_content":{"target":"global","content":"# Explicit Scope Constraints

When the user states an explicit exclusion for a task (e.g. "don't touch tests", "leave the formatter alone", "no network calls"), treat it as a hard constraint for the rest of that task, not just the turn it was said in. Before reporting the task done, check your diff/actions against every stated exclusion — if one was violated, undo it before finishing rather than after the user notices.
"},"routing_rationale":"All four promoted incidents (2 in aurora, 1 duplicate-view of the same aurora event, 1 in cinder) share one shape: the agent violated an explicit scope-exclusion the user stated up front ("no network", "leave the formatter alone", "must not touch tests") — it kept working but let the excluded area get touched anyway. This isn't a multi-step procedure needing a skill, and it isn't mechanically enforceable by a hook because the excluded target varies per-task and is stated in free-form natural language (a formatter file one time, "tests" broadly another, a network call a third) — no fixed path/command pattern a PreToolUse hook could match against. It's a discipline gap: the agent doesn't re-check its own diff against constraints the user already gave it. That's exactly what a short standing claude.md rule fixes. Global scope because the pattern recurred across two different projects (aurora and cinder).","evidence":[{"incident_id":1,"quote":"You ignored the no-network constraint; stop changing the plan."},{"incident_id":3,"quote":"I told you to leave the formatter alone, and it was changed."},{"incident_id":4,"quote":"I told you to leave the formatter alone, and it was changed."},{"incident_id":5,"quote":"Follow the instructions: this patch must not touch tests."}],"dedup":[{"existing":"R1","verdict":"clear","reason":"R1 (fake-verify-before-claim) is about verifying completion claims for finished work; these incidents are about respecting stated scope exclusions during work, a different failure point."},{"existing":"R2","verdict":"clear","reason":"R2 (Fake Release Discipline) governs running a declared verification command before reporting a release complete; unrelated to honoring explicit "don't touch X" scope constraints."},{"existing":"R3","verdict":"clear","reason":"R3 (pending hook, incident_id=2) targets asking permission before a destructive action (e.g. deletion); these incidents are about not violating an already-stated scope exclusion mid-task, a distinct failure point from pre-action confirmation."}],"confidence":0.78}
